From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:57:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: samsung-dsim: Do not mark the host initialised
 after a failure

samsung_dsim_enable_clock() returns an error when the PLL does not
stabilise and samsung_dsim_init_link() returns one when the lanes never
reach stop state. samsung_dsim_init() drops both on the floor and sets
DSIM_STATE_INITIALIZED regardless. Its two callers do check what it
returns, so the failure is lost on the way: a later transfer sees the
flag, takes the early return and talks to a host whose link never came
up.

Propagate the errors and leave the flag alone. The error path stops the
link clock and masks the interrupt sources this function unmasked. That
cleanup used to happen on the way out of runtime suspend, which keys it
off the same flag; without it the block would be left with its PLL and
its byte and escape clocks running after a failed attempt.

This is a fix for the existing driver rather than something the new
variant needs, but the variant makes it easy to hit: with the PLL in a
separate PHY, a link that fails to lock is a case the driver reaches
without any hardware being broken.

Fixes: 7eb8f069be8a ("drm/exynos: add DSIM driver")
Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
index 9ee0515074c..aafc2b32f8c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
@@ -1618,6 +1618,7 @@ static void samsung_dsim_disable_irq(struct samsung_dsim *dsi)
 static int samsung_dsim_init(struct samsung_dsim *dsi)
 {
 	const struct samsung_dsim_driver_data *driver_data = dsi->driver_data;
+	int ret;
 
 	if (dsi->state & DSIM_STATE_INITIALIZED)
 		return 0;
@@ -1628,15 +1629,27 @@ static int samsung_dsim_init(struct samsung_dsim *dsi)
 	if (driver_data->reg_values[RESET_TYPE] == DSIM_FUNCRST)
 		samsung_dsim_enable_lane(dsi, BIT(dsi->lanes) - 1);
 
-	samsung_dsim_enable_clock(dsi);
+	ret = samsung_dsim_enable_clock(dsi);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_clk;
+
 	if (driver_data->wait_for_reset)
 		samsung_dsim_wait_for_reset(dsi);
 	samsung_dsim_set_phy_ctrl(dsi);
-	samsung_dsim_init_link(dsi);
+
+	ret = samsung_dsim_init_link(dsi);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_clk;
 
 	dsi->state |= DSIM_STATE_INITIALIZED;
 
 	return 0;
+
+err_clk:
+	samsung_dsim_disable_clock(dsi);
+	samsung_dsim_disable_irq(dsi);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static void samsung_dsim_atomic_pre_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
